Falsifies `kernel::arch::aarch64::iommu::proofs::the_level_one_table_names_exactly_the_leaf`.

The defect is `SPAN` written as the leaf's size in bits, `SPLIT`, rather than `SPLIT + 1`. Arm
IHI 0070 counts a leaf as `2^(SPAN - 1)` STEs, so a `SPAN` of 6 tells the SMMU each leaf holds 32
and streams 32 to 63 of every leaf abort with `C_BAD_STE`. QEMU's walk reads the field as
`2^SPAN` entries (`max_l2_ste = (1 << span) - 1` in `hw/arm/smmuv3.c`), so under QEMU both values
pass and every test stays green; only silicon would show the half-leaf.

Expected to fail: `assert!(1u64 << ((descriptor & 0x1f) - 1) == STREAMS_PER_LEAF as u64, "SPAN
says the leaf holds exactly the streams one frame of STEs holds")`. Confirmed red on 2026-11-11
(UTC), on an x86_64 host, against this file's pure functions and harness compiled on their own.

The sibling harness `no_stream_can_reach_another_streams_tables` stays green under this patch:
it places streams and never builds a descriptor.

diff --git a/kernel/src/arch/aarch64/iommu.rs b/kernel/src/arch/aarch64/iommu.rs
--- a/kernel/src/arch/aarch64/iommu.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/arch/aarch64/iommu.rs
@@ -416,7 +416,7 @@
 /// Name: provisional.
 #[doc(alias = "L1STD")]
 const fn level_one_descriptor(leaf: u64) -> u64 {
-    (leaf & 0x000f_ffff_ffff_ffc0) | (STREAM_TABLE_SPLIT as u64 + 1)
+    (leaf & 0x000f_ffff_ffff_ffc0) | STREAM_TABLE_SPLIT as u64
 }
 
